WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.925
A few minutes later, the kids were in the main room facing the adults.

2
00:00:06.926 --> 00:00:10.775
Venna glared at the stowaways. "This is outrageous!

3
00:00:10.776 --> 00:00:13.812
The expedition is supposed to be top secret."

4
00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:18.368
"Does that mean we have to turn back?" Gliss sounded almost hopeful.

5
00:00:18.369 --> 00:00:24.237
"If so, the furies will have to rest for a few days before departing again," Tok warned.

6
00:00:24.238 --> 00:00:30.101
"Impossible." Venna frowned. "The king and queen won't appreciate any delay.

7
00:00:30.102 --> 00:00:35.475
Besides, there's no need to turn back. These kids can zap themselves home.

8
00:00:35.476 --> 00:00:39.110
We aren't close enough to the Cave yet to interfere with their magic."

9
00:00:39.111 --> 00:00:46.560
"No zapping," Tok said. "The furies will sense that level of magic. They'll get distracted and crash."

10
00:00:46.561 --> 00:00:54.911
Zann gulped. Tok had warned them earlier about not using any major magic during the journey. Now he understood why.

11
00:00:54.912 --> 00:00:59.506
"Perda and Darb will have to come with us then." Teplo glanced at Tok.

12
00:00:59.507 --> 00:01:02.030
"Is it safe to summon a message moth?

13
00:01:02.031 --> 00:01:04.800
We should let their parents know they're with us."

14
00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:09.425
"Yes, that minor sort of magic should be okay," Tok said.

15
00:01:09.426 --> 00:01:16.116
"We can't use magic?" Perda whispered to Zann. "It's like Morb is back again!"

16
00:01:16.117 --> 00:01:25.156
"Don't say that." Zann shuddered. "Let's explore the rest of the ship."

17
00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:28.022
"Prepare for landing!" Tok called out.

18
00:01:28.023 --> 00:01:34.474
Zann peered out the window. It was the next morning, and the sky was streaked with the remnants of sunrise.

19
00:01:34.475 --> 00:01:39.017
Below lay a vast desert littered with rocks and blowing red sand.

20
00:01:39.018 --> 00:01:44.549
Swirls of energy spurted out of a jagged opening, which looked like a mouth full of teeth.

21
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:48.499
"The Cave of the Unknown," Zann whispered.

22
00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:56.416
After hearing his parents talk about the place all his life, he was really here!

23
00:01:56.417 --> 00:02:02.846
As the group exited the aircraft, Tok warned everyone not to use magic in or around the Cave.

24
00:02:02.847 --> 00:02:06.232
"We've got something to help you. I'll fetch it now."

25
00:02:06.233 --> 00:02:11.694
"This place is amazing!" Perda said, staring at the cave opening in front of them.

26
00:02:11.695 --> 00:02:15.810
"Maybe we'll see some of the famous relics we learned about in school.

27
00:02:15.811 --> 00:02:20.629
Like the Mask of Zanta, or even the Horn of the Otherworld."

28
00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:25.304
Gliss shivered. "I'm not going in there. What if we get lost?

29
00:02:25.305 --> 00:02:28.887
We won't be able to use magic to find our way out."

30
00:02:28.888 --> 00:02:33.498
Teplo heard her. "Don't worry, that's what cave crawlers are for."

31
00:02:33.499 --> 00:02:36.210
"Cave crawlers?" Perda echoed.

32
00:02:36.211 --> 00:02:41.344
"Yes. Here they are." Tok had just returned, carrying a wire cage.

33
00:02:41.345 --> 00:02:48.557
Inside were a dozen large rodents with pale fur, long tails, and huge, glowing eyes.

34
00:02:48.558 --> 00:02:53.273
"Yuck!" Gliss said. "They look like swamp rats!"

35
00:02:53.274 --> 00:03:00.627
"You'll each get one," Tok said. "They're native to this area, so they know how to avoid the Cave's energy bursts.

36
00:03:00.628 --> 00:03:05.465
The glowworms they eat give their bodies a natural glow you can use as a light.

37
00:03:05.466 --> 00:03:10.623
And no matter how lost you get, your crawler can find the way out of the Cave." He

38
00:03:10.624 --> 00:03:16.167
set down the cage. Zing lunged toward it, shooting flames. "Zing,

39
00:03:16.168 --> 00:03:21.128
no!" said Zann, grabbing the dragon. He looked at Tok. "Sorry,

40
00:03:21.129 --> 00:03:26.349
I guess he thinks they're food. I hope he didn't scare them." "Once

41
00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:30.962
your crawler bonds to you, nothing will scare it off," Tok said. "Be

42
00:03:30.963 --> 00:03:34.871
careful not to let Zing actually catch one though." Tok

43
00:03:34.872 --> 00:03:38.975
placed a crawler on Zann's shoulder and muttered a quick spell. Even

44
00:03:38.976 --> 00:03:43.887
that little bit of magic made the energy storms intensify. "There,"

45
00:03:43.888 --> 00:03:48.144
said Tok. "This crawler is bonded to you now." The

46
00:03:48.145 --> 00:03:54.647
crawler dug its claws into Zann's shoulder and chirped nervously at Zing, who was watching it intently. Meanwhile

47
00:03:54.648 --> 00:03:58.815
Tok bonded crawlers to each of the other members of the group. "All

48
00:03:58.816 --> 00:04:05.538
right, everyone," Venna called out. "We'll begin by locating and cataloging each relic. I've

49
00:04:05.539 --> 00:04:12.232
drawn a diagram of the Cave based on the ancient texts and divided it into several sections." Venna

50
00:04:12.233 --> 00:04:15.709
continued to talk, but Zann stopped listening. "How

51
00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:24.428
can she make something as exciting as exploring the Cave of the Unknown sound so boring?" he whispered to his friends. He

52
00:04:24.429 --> 00:04:27.861
wondered what his parents' last journey to the Cave had been like. He

53
00:04:27.862 --> 00:04:33.223
stuck his hand into his pocket and touched the stone. To his surprise, it felt warm. "Weird,"

54
00:04:33.224 --> 00:04:35.365
he muttered. "What?"

55
00:04:35.366 --> 00:04:37.423
Perda asked. "Nothing."

56
00:04:37.424 --> 00:04:46.293
Zann shivered as he took a step toward the gaping cave mouth. "Let's go in." The

57
00:04:46.294 --> 00:04:49.294
kids spent the next hour exploring the Cave. Sounds

58
00:04:49.295 --> 00:04:52.408
echoed off the cold rock walls. Tiny,

59
00:04:52.409 --> 00:04:56.315
strange creatures scurried through the shadows. "Oops!"

60
00:04:56.316 --> 00:05:00.766
Perda blurted out as they crossed a large, shadowy chamber. "What's

61
00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.200
wrong?" Zann asked. "I

62
00:05:03.201 --> 00:05:10.346
tripped over a rock or something." Perda leaned down. "Actually, it looks like another relic." Gliss

63
00:05:10.347 --> 00:05:16.531
gasped. "Not just any relic. I think it's the Horn of the Otherworld!" "Careful!"

64
00:05:16.532 --> 00:05:23.439
Darb said. "Don't touch—whoa!" He skidded on some loose stones and fell. "Darb!

65
00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.762
Are you okay?" Gliss cried. "Sure.

66
00:05:26.763 --> 00:05:29.408
I just skinned my knee." Gliss

67
00:05:29.409 --> 00:05:35.103
hurried over. "Let me see." She rubbed her fingers to do a Healing spell. "No

68
00:05:35.104 --> 00:05:37.696
magic!" Zann shouted. It

69
00:05:37.697 --> 00:05:44.560
was too late. Energy crackled from Gliss' fingertips, and the Horn lit up. Zann felt the air sizzle. Zap

70
00:05:44.561 --> 00:05:47.019
!

71
00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:50.945
"Ow!" he exclaimed, landing hard in a different tunnel.

72
00:05:50.946 --> 00:05:53.808
A second later his friends landed beside him.

73
00:05:53.809 --> 00:05:56.399
"What happened?" Gliss cried.

74
00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:02.401
"You used magic," Perda said. "The Horn must have zapped us away!"

75
00:06:02.402 --> 00:06:05.388
"Where are we?" Gliss sounded panicky.

76
00:06:05.389 --> 00:06:09.982
"Don't worry," Darb said. "Our crawlers can find the way out."

77
00:06:09.983 --> 00:06:13.495
Zann cocked his head. "Maybe they won't have to.

78
00:06:13.496 --> 00:06:17.342
I hear someone talking. We must have landed near the entrance."

79
00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.638
He hurried in the direction of the voice.

80
00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:21.797
It was coming from the next chamber.

81
00:06:21.798 --> 00:06:25.519
"Hello," Zann called as he entered the chamber. "We—"

82
00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:29.040
Zann took one look at the speaker and gasped.

83
00:06:29.041 --> 00:06:33.203
It was Morb!

